__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
# ...except a brief's own proof artifacts. A gate verdict is only worth what
# someone else can re-check, and `*.log` was silently swallowing 32 evidence
# files across briefs 003-005: brief 003 is ACCEPT 9/9 in the working tree
# and REJECT on a fresh clone of the same commit, because 14 of the 54 files
# its manifest declares are not in version control. A rule written for build
# noise was eating the proof.
!harness/queue/briefs/**/deliverables/evidence/
!harness/queue/briefs/**/deliverables/evidence/**

# Per-machine permission overrides. Until now this file was untracked AND
# unignored, so the effective permission set was neither auditable nor
# reviewable -- it pre-approved `Bash(py -c ' *)`, i.e. arbitrary code
# execution, on one machine only and in no one's diff.
.claude/settings.local.json

# A Cursor run killed before its trap fires leaves the parked settings here,
# and the repository running with no hooks at all. Never commit that state:
# harness/tests/test_hooks_armed.py fails for as long as this file exists.
.claude/settings.json.cursor-hook-bug-disabled
